                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, indeed, installing from GitLab is possible, but with a caveat. For example, installing [this plugin](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab.vim) showed warning that link needs `.git` suffix, but plugin still correctly installs. Here is the full code snippet (with `later` lazy-loading):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nMiniDeps.later(\r\n  function()\r\n    MiniDeps.add({\r\n      source = 'https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab.vim.git',\r\n      name = 'gitlab.vim',\r\n    })\r\n  end\r\n)\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, indeed, installing from GitLab is possible, but with a caveat. For example, installing <a href=\"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab.vim\" rel=\"nofollow\">this plugin</a> showed warning that link needs <code class=\"notranslate\">.git</code> suffix, but plugin still correctly installs. Here is the full code snippet (with <code class=\"notranslate\">later</code> lazy-loading):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"MiniDeps.later(\n  function()\n    MiniDeps.add({\n      source = 'https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab.vim.git',\n      name = 'gitlab.vim',\n    })\n  end\n)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniDeps</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">later</span>(\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniDeps</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">add</span>({\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab.vim.git<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>gitlab.vim<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n    })\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n)</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, indeed, installing from GitLab is possible, but with a caveat. For example, installing this plugin showed warning that link needs .git suffix, but plugin still correctly installs. Here is the full code snippet (with later lazy-loading):\nMiniDeps.later(\n  function()\n    MiniDeps.add({\n      source = 'https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/editor-extensions/gitlab.vim.git',\n      name = 'gitlab.vim',\n    })\n  end\n)",
